<speak>
<s>From <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news, this is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">24022026</say-as>.</s> <s>The seventh of <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="rɑmɑˈdˤɑːn">Ramadan</phoneme>, fourteen forty-seven.</s> <s>It's evening in <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈmæk.kæ">Makkah</phoneme>, between <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="mɑɣrɪb">Maghrib</phoneme> and <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ʕɪʃæːʔ">Isha</phoneme>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<s>Lebanon's army command has ordered soldiers to reinforce a military post near <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="mɑrˌdʒɑˈjuːn">Marjayoun</phoneme> and return fire on Israeli forces, the first such order since the ceasefire that post was built to enforce.</s> <s>Israel still occupies five positions in southern Lebanon in violation of that truce, and a sovereign Arab army now has standing orders to shoot back.</s> <s>The next incident risks the first direct firefight between the Israeli military and Lebanese regular forces since the ceasefire took hold.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>At the International Criminal Court, prosecutors played video of former Philippine president Rodrigo <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="duːˈtɛrteɪ">Duterte</phoneme> declaring, in his own words, that he alone bore responsibility for the drug war.</s> <s>The hearing covers seventy-six documented killings, a fraction of the estimated twelve to thirty thousand dead, and includes testimony that police strangled children with packing tape over their heads.</s> <s>Duterte is the first Southeast Asian head of state to stand before the court.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>India buys more Israeli weapons than any other country, and during Prime Minister Narendra Modi's visit to Jerusalem, Benjamin Netanyahu announced a six-nation alliance against what he called radical axes, linking Israel, India, and unnamed Arab and Asian states.</s> <s>The announcement builds on a November defense pact and deepens an alignment between two governments facing mounting international scrutiny over their military occupations and treatment of Muslim minorities.</s> <s>Israel's parliamentary opposition boycotted Modi's address to the <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈknɛ.sɛt">Knesset</phoneme>.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>North Korea's first Workers' Party congress in five years formally elevated <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="kɪm joˈdʒɔŋ">Kim Yo-jong</phoneme> to department director, placing on paper a role she has wielded in the shadows as her brother's closest adviser.</s> <s>Her return to the politburo marks the first formal acknowledgment of a hierarchy long assumed by outside analysts, and confirms she stands second in the regime.</s> <s>The congress is expected to set nuclear doctrine and military spending for the years ahead.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In conflict and security.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>In eastern Democratic Republic of Congo, a government drone strike killed the military spokesman of the Rwandan-backed March 23 Movement.</s> <s>The group controls the <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ruːˈbɑː.jɑ">Rubaya</phoneme> coltan mine supplying roughly fifteen percent of the world's tantalum, the mineral inside every smartphone.</s> <s>Simultaneous strikes hit three further positions the same morning, signaling a coordinated offensive to retake the mineral-rich east.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Iran is acquiring China's CM-302 supersonic cruise missile, a weapon designed to sink aircraft carriers, giving Tehran a strike range of two hundred and ninety kilometres against the two United States carrier groups now deployed in the region.</s> <s>Six independent sources confirmed the deal, which involves China's state-owned aerospace industry.</s> <s>Indirect nuclear talks are scheduled in Geneva on Thursday, and the missile acquisition reshapes what Iran brings to those negotiations.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Al-Qaeda-linked fighters have pushed to the five-hundred-kilometre Mali-Senegal border, the furthest west jihadist groups have reached in West Africa.</s> <s>The Group for the Support of Islam and Muslims expanded exponentially into southwestern Mali after military juntas expelled French forces, leaving ungoverned territory along the porous frontier.</s> <s>Senegal has reinforced its border, but with Côte d'Ivoire and Ghana now in the movement's sightlines, the coastal belt may be the next front.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Israeli settlers shot three Palestinians in the West Bank village of <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈmuːx.mɑs">Mukhmas</phoneme>, killing a teenager.</s> <s>Witnesses described Israeli soldiers standing nearby, smoking, while the attack unfolded, part of a documented pattern in which the military has protected settlers through deliberate inaction.</s> <s>No arrests have been made, for this killing or for a separate settler assault the week before.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Nigeria's central bank cut its benchmark interest rate from twenty-seven to twenty-six and a half percent, citing inflation falling to fifteen point one percent in January.</s> <s>The relief is limited: at twenty-six and a half percent, borrowing remains a crisis-level burden, and banks must still hold forty-five percent of deposits in reserve, shrinking the pool of available credit further.</s> <s>For a country where a hundred and thirty-three million people live in poverty, the adjustment changes the headline number without changing the underlying reality.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>German car exports to China fell another third in 2025, dropping below fourteen billion euros, roughly half the thirty billion peak of twenty twenty-two.</s> <s>Chinese automakers have come to dominate their home market, especially in electric vehicles, at a pace German engineers did not anticipate, and the German Economic Institute sees no path back to the previous market share.</s> <s>Chancellor <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈfriːdrɪç mɛrts">Friedrich Merz</phoneme> visited Beijing this week, but the structural shift in the world's largest car market appears permanent.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Archaeologists dating the <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="uːˌbeɪˈdiː.jɑ">Ubeidiya</phoneme> site in Israel have placed two distinct human ancestor species, Homo erectus and Homo habilis, at the same location two million years ago, four hundred thousand years before the accepted date for humanity's first migration out of Africa.</s> <s>Their tools appearing in the same rock layer means the two species did not leave separately, but together, through the Levant corridor, the only land bridge connecting Africa to Eurasia at the time.</s> <s>Researchers say every archaeological site along that route now needs to be re-examined with the revised timeline in mind.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>After more than a month occupying Cargill's grain port on Brazil's <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˌtɑ.pɑˈʒɔs">Tapajós</phoneme> River, indigenous communities forced a government reversal.</s> <s>Brazil revoked the decree permitting dredging of the river for soy exports, after communities argued the waterway is central to their food security and survival, a decision that came days after Brazil's soy industry quietly withdrew its lobbying push.</s> <s>It is a rare case of sustained direct action halting an extraction project backed by one of the world's most powerful agricultural lobbies.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>China's DeepSeek trained its next model on Nvidia's Blackwell chip, hardware that United States export controls explicitly bar from entering China, a breach confirmed by a senior Trump administration official who declined to say how the chips reached DeepSeek's facility in Inner Mongolia.</s> <s>That same week, Beijing sanctioned forty Japanese defense firms including Mitsubishi Heavy Industries, banning dual-use arms and radar exports in retaliation after Tokyo suggested a Taiwan attack could justify Japanese military action.</s> <s>Together the two moves represent a coordinated challenge to the architecture of Western export controls, one breaching them from within, the other striking back from outside.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Robotics companies are marketing humanoid machines as autonomous while quietly employing people to operate them remotely.</s> <s>The startup 1X plans to sell its twenty-thousand-dollar Neo robot to homes this year without committing to any level of self-operation, and other firms use workers in motion-capture suits as hidden data collectors.</s> <s>The pattern mirrors the early years of self-driving cars, and raises the question of when, or whether, these systems will ever run without a person in the loop.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<s>That's your briefing from <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news.</s>
<break time="500ms"/>
<s>We're back in eleven hours.</s>
<break time="300ms"/>
<s><phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ʔɪn ʃæːʔ ɑɫ.ɫɑːh">إن شاء الله</phoneme>.</s>
</speak>